# Vanilla: Expanded TODO List:
    ## Issues:
        ☐ Add "sheltered" indicator which shows whether the player is protected from the elements.
        ☐ BUG: Quern auto stash not working for items which the base game prefers not to merge (e.g. perishable foods which have a large difference in freshness). FIX: the quern should force merge items when auto stashing.
        ☐ Design a better separation of alloy calculator inventory ownership/liveness validation, transfer permissions, and storage-versus-machine access policy. Reconsider the storage-class whitelist without weakening ownership or withdrawal checks, and define coverage for vanilla and modded containers.
        ☐ Prevent "Equip light source" hotkey from triggering when the player is holding a hammer and has tongs equipped in offhand.

    ## New Features:
        ☐ Add a "Todo List" feature which allows players to create their own ingame tasks and reminders.
        ☐ Targeted items such as tools on toolracks have a subtle highlight to indicate that they are targeted.
        ☐ New "crafting menu" similar to minecraft: shows all craftable items with current inventory, allows searching. (Maybe this can just be added to the handbook?)

    ## Death Penalties:
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *bag* items on death (items in inventory are lost, items on hotbar and equipped armor and weapons are kept).
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *unequipped* items on death (items in inventory and hotbar are lost, equipped armor and weapons are kept).
        ☐ New death penalty option: lose *all* items on death (items in inventory, hotbar, equipped armor & weapons are lost).
        ☐ Tool degradation on death: all tools in inventory and hotbar lose <configurable percent> durability on death.

    ## Effects:
        ☐ Blocks with light level 1 have subtle haze/smoke particles (to indicate the edge of lit areas) (reuse the existing temporal storm ground particle effect).

# Vanilla: Rebalanced Ideas:
    Note: this is a different mod from Vanilla: Expanded, I'm just keeping the ideas list here for now.
    ## Recipes:
        ☐ Candles from animal fat (render fat into tallow -> tallow replaces wax in candle recipe).

    ## Monster Rebalancing:
        ☐ Monsters cant spawn under roofs.
        ☐ Increase gear drop rates from monsters (and trading costs for gears) by 500%. this will make fighting monsters feel more rewarding.
        ☐ Add other items to monster drops (bones, scrapmetal, metal parts (uncommon), gems (rare), etc) to make them more rewarding to fight.
